{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Cruithne","id":"150319814836092928","is_bot":0,"username":"cruithne"},"author_id":"150319814836092928","channel_id":"863491404835586108","content":"(since I'm not doing anything today but I want to set my location\nI don't know how visible each individual airship is from the dock, but in case it's visible enough that people can see)\nSabrine is staring out of the window of the Nightingale, looking almost like a mannequin to any passers-by, before they realise that no, she's just lost in thought or meditation. What looks like a four-winged raven perches on the roof, watching as people enter and leave the dock.","created_at":"2021-07-10T18:59:16.086000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"863494602064265246","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Cruithne","id":"150319814836092928","is_bot":0,"username":"cruithne"},"author_id":"150319814836092928","channel_id":"863491404835586108","content":"The Nightingale itself is rather more battered than the average docked airship - not that that's saying much. Peeling paint depicts the airship's name, and one plank looks significantly different to the others - paint on the planks above and below show what looks to be parts of letters, though scrubbed off to the point that no clue exists to any letter on the original plank. Its singular window is cracked, and in places there are fresh-looking webs.","created_at":"2021-07-10T19:11:59.450000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"863497803846516785","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
