{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Cruithne","id":"150319814836092928","is_bot":0,"username":"cruithne"},"author_id":"150319814836092928","channel_id":"863491404835586108","content":"(currently under the assumption I have to go physically deliver it)\nshe folds up the paper and puts it in a pouch. ||This is an article about... earlier's events... for the city post. However - I would rather not take it myself in case I get recognised - I don't believe I would, but just in case.||","created_at":"2021-07-12T12:41:02.895000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"864124195654991902","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Cruithne","id":"150319814836092928","is_bot":0,"username":"cruithne"},"author_id":"150319814836092928","channel_id":"863491404835586108","content":"||As such - I would appreciate if you could take it. If we walk separately, then even if I were arrested, you would likely slip by and be able to submit it on my behalf. If it gets published I will of course compensate you for the risk, but I have no guarantee...||","created_at":"2021-07-12T12:42:02.481000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"864124445576527873","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Cruithne","id":"150319814836092928","is_bot":0,"username":"cruithne"},"author_id":"150319814836092928","channel_id":"863491404835586108","content":"(and then we got yeeted to the post so)\n\n***The Journal of Sabrine Lovlatar, pg. 1***\n\n*Without Kukudh, I require a way to calm my thoughts before I rest. This shall have to suffice.*\n*Kukudh... my guide. What am I to do without them? How am I to navigate this chaotic city, this chaotic world?*\n\n*But no. There is hope. I am seen as an ally to some, and maybe even a friend... Kukudh sacrificed themselves to save an ally, after all. And I will make sure they all are honoured - though anonymously - as they should be.*\n*And with this word, 'familiar', it seems those like Kukudh are not as rare as I thought. Perhaps they can return to me.*\n*The newspaper requested that I and another collaborate on two articles. It appears Hampstead is the only area actively hostile to people, although it depends on if they would see me as 'people'.*\n\n*There was a dinosaur en route to Ferrytown. A surprisingly friendly creature for its size, and a fascinating one. And the bugs! So small, yet so synchronised!*\n\n*Roy and I went to the Ferrytown games. I won nothing, but after the Incident I cannot be surprised. Especially as I tried... (The journal trails off here, to restart in noticeably worse handwriting.)*\n\n*i was seen. but it was alright. but it was only one aspect...*","created_at":"2021-07-12T20:19:45.961000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"864239635760283669","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Cruithne","id":"150319814836092928","is_bot":0,"username":"cruithne"},"author_id":"150319814836092928","channel_id":"863491404835586108","content":"(alright, so here's what I'm going to do, I cleared it with Rob - to get around time zones, while I'm going to go to bed momentarily, Sabrine will still be working for a bit longer, getting quotes for Luard (either he'll grab them when people are online or just work something out); assuming I don't act tomorrow until 8am my time (it's 10:25pm), that's an hour and a half for Sabrine to obtain interviews and still get her designated long rest time\nI'll run longrest command when I go to bed, but Sabrine won't act until 8am my time at the earliest)\n\nafter filling in the entry, Sabrine starts preparing for her work to come.","created_at":"2021-07-12T20:26:45.701000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-12T20:27:27.276000Z","id":"864241396277706762","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
